## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-region, multi-account disaster recovery with auditable controls, automated failover, and safe rollback for a live telemetry stack.

## Key Concepts
- Active-passive DR patterns with RTO/RPO trade-offs
- Cross-region data flows: Kinesis replication via Lambda consumers, S3 Cross-Region Replication, OpenSearch Cross-Cluster Replication
- DNS-based failover using Route 53 Application Recovery Controller with health checks
- Infrastructure as Code-driven recovery runbooks with automated rollback capabilities
- Regular testing cadence with documented rollback procedures and audit trails

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Cross-region Kinesis replication trigger handler
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const records = event.Records;
  const firehoseClient = new AWS.Firehose({region: 'eu-central-1'});

  for (const record of records) {
    await firehoseClient.putRecord({
      DeliveryStreamName: 'dr-telemetry-stream',
      Record: { Data: record.kinesis.data }
    }).promise();
  }
};
```
